cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pycuf in research or professional work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "pycuf: read, check and analyse CUF-XML construction cost estimates"
abstract: >-
  pycuf is a Python library that reads CUF-XML (Calculatie Uitwissel Formaat), the Dutch
  exchange format for construction cost estimates, into a typed model. It computes costs with
  exact decimals under explicit, configurable interpretation policies, reports structural and
  calculation problems as graded, coded findings instead of refusing to load a file, and exports
  normalized tables to CSV, JSONL, Arrow, polars, pandas and Parquet. The core has no
  dependencies outside the Python standard library.
authors:
